{
  "format": "jekray",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Optical differentiator: a 4f Fourier filter",
  "snap": 1,
  "maxBounces": 200,
  "minPower": 0.1,
  "ghosts": false,
  "library": [],
  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "laser",
      "type": "source",
      "name": "Laser, 532 nm",
      "x": -260,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 0,
      "wavelength": 532,
      "colourAuto": true,
      "colour": "#65ff00",
      "width": 6,
      "divergence": 0,
      "gauss": true,
      "w0": 3,
      "z0": 0,
      "beamView": "field",
      "beamScale": "lin",
      "popN": 256,
      "popModel": "auto",
      "traceRays": true,
      "pol": "s",
      "polAngle": 45,
      "lines": [],
      "rays": 3,
      "power": 10,
      "coh": 0,
      "splitFrom": null,
      "splitPhase": 0,
      "splitPath": 0,
      "lineshape": "lorentz",
      "m2": 1,
      "tem": "gauss",
      "hm": 1,
      "hn": 0,
      "lp": 0,
      "ll": 1,
      "tau": 0,
      "pshape": "sech2",
      "rep": 80,
      "gdd0": 0,
      "sweeps": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "input_mask",
      "type": "mask",
      "name": "Input f(x)",
      "x": -200,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 0,
      "length": 25.4,
      "amp": "0.6*cos(2*pi*x/1.5)+0.4*sin(2*pi*x/0.5)",
      "delay": "0",
      "preset": "custom",
      "sweeps": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "input_screen",
      "type": "screen",
      "name": "Input",
      "x": -170,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 180,
      "length": 12,
      "absorb": false,
      "R": null,
      "binWidth": 0,
      "binInterp": true,
      "mapScale": "lin",
      "vectorFocus": "auto",
      "trap": "none",
      "trapF": "avg",
      "trapMat": "Fused silica",
      "trapR": 100,
      "trapRho": 2200,
      "trapMed": "bench",
      "trapP": 1013.25,
      "trapT": 295,
      "mtfFreq": 50,
      "abSrc": "",
      "abAng": 2,
      "abH": 1,
      "abN": 7,
      "abRays": 61,
      "sweeps": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "lens1",
      "type": "mask",
      "name": "L1, f 100 mm",
      "x": -100,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 0,
      "length": 25.4,
      "amp": "1",
      "delay": "-(sqrt(r^2+10000)-100)/lambda",
      "preset": "custom",
      "sweeps": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "fourier_screen",
      "type": "screen",
      "name": "Fourier plane",
      "x": -2,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 180,
      "length": 2,
      "absorb": false,
      "R": null,
      "binWidth": 0,
      "binInterp": true,
      "mapScale": "lin",
      "vectorFocus": "auto",
      "trap": "none",
      "trapF": "avg",
      "trapMat": "Fused silica",
      "trapR": 100,
      "trapRho": 2200,
      "trapMed": "bench",
      "trapP": 1013.25,
      "trapT": 295,
      "mtfFreq": 50,
      "abSrc": "",
      "abAng": 2,
      "abH": 1,
      "abN": 7,
      "abRays": 61,
      "sweeps": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "fourier_mask",
      "type": "mask",
      "name": "Ramp, H ∝ k",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 0,
      "length": 25.4,
      "amp": "max(-1,min(1,x/0.125))",
      "delay": "0",
      "preset": "custom",
      "sweeps": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "lens2",
      "type": "mask",
      "name": "L2, f 100 mm",
      "x": 100,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 0,
      "length": 25.4,
      "amp": "1",
      "delay": "-(sqrt(r^2+10000)-100)/lambda",
      "preset": "custom",
      "sweeps": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "output",
      "type": "screen",
      "name": "Output",
      "x": 200,
      "y": 0,
      "angle": 180,
      "length": 12,
      "absorb": true,
      "R": null,
      "binWidth": 0,
      "binInterp": true,
      "mapScale": "lin",
      "vectorFocus": "auto",
      "trap": "none",
      "trapF": "avg",
      "trapMat": "Fused silica",
      "trapR": 100,
      "trapRho": 2200,
      "trapMed": "bench",
      "trapP": 1013.25,
      "trapT": 295,
      "mtfFreq": 50,
      "abSrc": "",
      "abAng": 2,
      "abH": 1,
      "abN": 7,
      "abRays": 61,
      "sweeps": {}
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Spatial differentiation with a Fourier filter. A 4f system: lens L1 turns the light leaving the input mask into its spatial spectrum on the Fourier plane, where a spatial frequency ν lands at x = λfν (532 nm × 100 mm: 0.053 mm for each line per mm); the Fourier mask weights each frequency; L2 turns the result back. Both lenses are ideal (masks with a perfect-lens delay), so the only filtering is the mask's. The input is two tones under the broad Gaussian beam, f(x) = 0.6 cos(2πx/1.5 mm) + 0.4 sin(2πx/0.5 mm), with no constant part; a negative amplitude is a phase of π, so a mask can carry a signed field. Its spectrum is four spots on the Fourier plane, at ±0.035 mm (the 1.5 mm tone) and ±0.106 mm (the 0.5 mm one). The output is the filtered input imaged upside down: x becomes −x. Open each screen's Diffraction tab and choose Profiles to compare the input, the spots on the Fourier plane and the output. Differentiating multiplies each frequency by i·2πν, so the mask is a ramp in amplitude, H(x) = x / 0.125 mm (held to ±1 so it stays passive), signed: the two sides of the spectrum leave with opposite signs, and the i is a constant phase that the intensity does not show. The output is then f′(−x) under the beam: −0.6 k₁ sin(k₁x) + 0.4 k₂ cos(k₂x) with k = 2π/period, where the 0.5 mm tone, three times the frequency, comes out three times as strong against the other. So the fine fringes dominate the output; the optical integrator does the opposite. The beam's own Gaussian edge is differentiated too, adding a small term where the light falls off."
}
